      "title": "Questions about the subject",
      "summary": "When the question word is the subject, the word order does not change.",
      "status": "draft",
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "What it is",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "When the question word is the subject of the sentence, there is no auxiliary and the word order does not change."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Who** called?",
                "**What** happened?",
                "**Which** train leaves first?"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "How it works in English",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraphs",
              "paragraphs": [
                "Compare Who called you? (who is the subject) with Who did you call? (who is the object). Only the object question needs do."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "html": "<table><thead><tr><th>Subject question</th><th>Object question</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Who called you?</strong></td><td><strong>Who did you call?</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>What fell?</strong></td><td><strong>What did you drop?</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
